WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.640
Between the client and server.

2
00:00:08.649 --> 00:00:11.670
There is a system for synchronizing and acknowledging any

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.880
request that is known as a three way handshake.

4
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:20.719
This handshake is used to establish a TCP connection between two devices.

5
00:00:21.709 --> 00:00:23.879
Here we will take a simplified look at

6
00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:27.020
how communications are established to a web server.

7
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:29.569
Depending on the exact protocol.

8
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.080
There may be additional connection negotiation taking place

9
00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:39.270
first, the client sends synchronization sin packet to the web servers.

10
00:00:39.279 --> 00:00:41.709
Port 80 or 443.

11
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.650
This is a request to establish a connection.

12
00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:54.400
The web server replies to the sin packet with an acknowledgment known as a sin

13
00:00:55.009 --> 00:00:55.020
A.

14
00:00:58.139 --> 00:01:01.970
Finally, the client acknowledges the connection with an acknowledgment

15
00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:02.549
ac

16
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:02.779
at

17
00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.089
this point,

18
00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:06.970
the basic connection is established and the client and

19
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.169
host will further negotiate secure communications over that connection.